BEGIN_PGML A famous fact about such a triangle is that [`c=\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\text{.}`] So if one leg [`a`] is [$a] inches long, and if the perimeter is [$p] inches long, then we have an equation [`[$left]=[$right]\text{.}`] Is the other leg [`[$proposed_solution]`] inches long?
>> [@DataTable( [ [ PGML('[`[$left->TeX]`]'), PGML('[`=`]'), PGML('[`[$right->TeX]`]'), ], [ PGML('[_]{$lefteval}{3}'), PGML('[`\wonder{=}`]'), PGML('[`[$righteval->TeX]`]'), ], ], align => 'rcl', valign => 'middle',);@]* <<
[_]{$dropdown}{5}
END_PGML
